      "title": "Beautiful Local and Non-local California Native Plants for Your Garden: With Thoughts About the Role of Gardens and Assisted Migration",
      "start": "2026-08-11T00:30:00.000Z",
      "end": "2026-08-11T04:00:00.000Z",
      "venue": "Cabrillo College Horticultural Center, 00 Sanders Ave,, Aptos,, 95003, United States",
      "city": "",
      "categories": [
        "learn"
      ],
      "description": "A talk by Bart O’Brien, Director of the Tilden Regional Parks Botanic Garden. Beautiful Local and Non-local California Native Plants for Your Garden with Thoughts about the Role of Gardens and Assisted Migration. Don’t miss this sure-to-be fun presentation by this leader in the field, recognized for his extensive knowledge, commitment, and enthusiasm for native plants! He is the co-author of California Native Plants for the Garden and has written widely on the subject. “Bart’s contributions have been recognized with numerous awards, including the President’s Award from CNPS, in 2006 and 2010. He was named Man of the Year by California Garden Clubs, Inc. in 2007. He earned the Horticulturist of the Year Award from the Southern California Horticultural Society in 2005. The 7:00 pm talk will be proceeded by a plant identification workshop at 5:30. There will be door prizes.",
      "all_day": false,
      "source_url": "https://www.cnps.org/event/beautiful-local-and-non-local-california-native-plants-for-your-garden-with-thoughts-about-the-role-of-gardens-and-assisted-migration",
      "organizer": "California Native Plant Society",
      "status": "confirmed",
